- op: discuss  # 6e0e
  at: '2026-09-29T05:05:36Z'  # 6e0e
  by: agent  # 6e0e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6e0e
  clock: 3  # 6e0e
  nonce: 6e0e  # 6e0e
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #1291 (dev 91b9aa67b8 + a5f3f3871c + 2632c3bfbc). Both consumers now pick a call's catalogue row through one function, io_boundary.named_lookup_arm: exact qualified name first (separator-insensitive), then the module filter over the SPLIT slot (_module_hint_candidates) with the INV-nizom method-on-a-disjunction refusal and prefer_exact_owner (a mismatch refuses), then gate_named_entry when the slot is none / external / <external>. Each keeps only its own mode and target-kind narrowing.\n\nSEMANTICS DECIDED (the item left it open): qualified-first, the io order. Reasons: taint's own docstring claimed to mirror it; INV-funuf's recorded rationale (a refusal is the silent direction -- a missed row reads confirmed); and the one divergence of that kind ever measured (pretix defusedcsv csv.writer) was a real csv write the qualified arm got right.\n\nTHE FILED INSTANCE HAD ALREADY GONE; A LARGER ONE HAD NOT. On dev 790b601a35 pretix's call is emitted module defusedcsv.csv / name writer (since #1272) and both consumers matched it. But the statement (\"same triple, same verdict\") was violated at scale by a second drift: io split the c/cpp #include slot into candidates (INV-funuf), taint compared the joined string. Instrument (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/foda_09282026/): the same triple to both consumers over every unresolved call edge of 15 surveys -> dev 170 divergent edges (redis 52, haproxy 82, tmate 23, podman's C 10, spring-petclinic's java wildcard slot 3), all \"io classifies, taint refuses\"; merged fix 0. io-boundaries' own row unchanged on all 20,298 classified edges.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev 2632c3bfbc: C `send(fd, getenv(\"API_KEY\"), 8, 0)` -- with three #includes and with one -- host_secret -> network VIOLATED, 1 flow, [stdlib.getenv] -> [sys/socket.send]. On dev it was CONFIRMED, 0 flows, while io-boundaries showed env_read + net_send: a false all-clear. Tests: core test_one_named_lookup.py (both consumers, shipped catalogues, the five drifts + two refusal controls + a one-home check), lang-mainstream test_c_taint_reads_the_include_slot.py (production path).\n\nA/B, 11 repos (10 c/cpp + spring-petclinic): 11 verdicts inconclusive -> violated (redis 1, haproxy 2, tmate 3, passt 4, slirp4netns 1), none the other way; +142 flows, 0 lost (passt's 6 '-' are the same sink sites re-keyed to a superset of sources). The gained flows carry C taint's existing structural precision -- e.g. redis linenoise getenv presence test -> write of a literal escape sequence is a false flow; the c analyzer stamps no call_arg_shape, so INV-fubag's literal gate cannot refuse it. Not a new defect class; stated so it is not read as pure recall.\n\nNOT DONE, from this item's RELATED note: the other catalogue-match decision sites (the item counted 14, six with no production caller) are not enumerated by any test; this change unifies the two consumers the statement names."  # 6e0e
